[
    "5.4. Linux-6.16.1 API Headers",
    "<a id=\"ch-tools-linux-headers\" name=\"ch-tools-linux-headers\"></a>5.4. Linux-6.16.1 API Headers",
    "The Linux API Headers (in linux-6.16.1.tar.xz) expose the kernel's API for use by Glibc.",
    "Approximate build time:",
    "less than 0.1 SBU",
    "Required disk space:",
    "1.7 GB",
    "5.4.1. Installation of Linux API Headers",
    "The Linux kernel needs to expose an Application Programming Interface (API) for the system's C library (Glibc in LFS) to use. This is done by way of sanitizing various C header files that are shipped in the Linux kernel source tarball.",
    "Make sure there are no stale files embedded in the package:",
    "Now extract the user-visible kernel headers from the source. The recommended make target <span class=\"quote\">“<span class=\"quote\">headers_install</span>”</span> cannot be used, because it requires <span class=\"application\">rsync</span>, which may not be available. The headers are first placed in <code class=\"filename\">./usr</code>, then copied to the needed location.",
    "<a id=\"contents-linux-headers\" name=\"contents-linux-headers\"></a>5.4.2. Contents of Linux API Headers",
    "Installed headers:",
    "/usr/include/asm/*.h, /usr/include/asm-generic/*.h, /usr/include/drm/*.h, /usr/include/linux/*.h, /usr/include/misc/*.h, /usr/include/mtd/*.h, /usr/include/rdma/*.h, /usr/include/scsi/*.h, /usr/include/sound/*.h, /usr/include/video/*.h, and /usr/include/xen/*.h",
